    "title": "Police investigating triple shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago NORTH ST. LOUIS COUNTY (First Alert 4) - Police are investigating a triple shooting that happened in North County Wednesday evening. The shooting happened around 8:30 p.m. in the parking lot of a business in the 2900 block of Patterson Road, which is near the border of Florissant and unincorporated St. Louis County. The victims then drove to the 900 block of Lindbergh Blvd in Florissant, where police were called. Read full article\n1",
